WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.350
A medical practice signs with dozens
of vendors: athenahealth for records,

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.800
Weave for the phones, Stericycle for
medical waste, Henry Schein for supplies.

3
00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.780
Connexcy keeps every contract
and invoice in one place,

4
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.100
with each vendor's business associate
agreement right next to it,

5
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.870
and pulls out the dates and
prices. A person checks every one.

6
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.610
Your athenahealth agreement
renews next September,

7
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:30.170
with 120 days' notice. Changing
records systems takes months,

8
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.620
so Connexcy alerts your practice
administrator a full year ahead.

9
00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:38.960
Every invoice is matched to its contract.
Still paying for two clinicians

10
00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:43.890
who left in the spring? Connexcy flags
it, so the seats come off the bill.

11
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.870
Before Weave renews, compare it with
other patient messaging vendors,

12
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.110
and read the notes on why you chose it.

13
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.360
Then it goes to the administrator,
the medical director and the CFO.

14
00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:58.680
Connexcy for healthcare
practices. Every contract.

15
00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:03.850
Every invoice. Connected. Join
the beta at connexcy.com.
